---
import '../styles/fraunces.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '../styles/global.css';
import RoomNerve from '../components/RoomNerve.astro';
import RoomShell from '../components/RoomShell.astro';

const specimens = [
  {
    src: '/cabinet/umbrella-elephant-cutout.png',
    no: '01',
    title: 'The weather keeper',
    meta: 'Elephant · umbrella · impossible poise',
    alt: 'A seated figure with an elephant head holding an umbrella',
  },
  {
    src: '/cabinet/goldfish-source.png',
    no: '02',
    title: 'A thought in suspension',
    meta: 'Goldfish · memory · interior worlds',
    alt: 'A goldfish held in a dark interior',
  },
  {
    src: '/cabinet/keepsake-brain-cutout.png',
    no: '03',
    title: 'The portable cabinet',
    meta: 'Brain · keepsakes · collected matter',
    alt: 'A brain form filled with small keepsakes',
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Context · EDUARDO sopalda</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <RoomNerve current="/context" heading={false} />
    <RoomShell title="Context" italic="a small history.">
      <section class="open">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">An opening specimen</p>
          <p class="display">Before knowledge had departments, the world could still sit in one room.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="hero-plate">
          <img src="/cabinet/umbrella-elephant-cutout.png" alt="A seated figure with an elephant head holding an umbrella" />
          <figcaption>One room trying to hold the world</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="block">
        <p class="kicker">01 · Before the departments</p>
        <h2>A room for the almost unbelievable.</h2>
        <p>
          In early modern Europe, a <em>Wunderkammer</em> — a chamber of wonder — or <em>Kunstkammer</em>
          gathered natural things, human-made marvels and instruments under one roof.
        </p>
        <p>
          Shell beside astrolabe. Fossil beside carved ivory. Not a catalogue of the strange: a small,
          imperfect world assembled to be looked at, argued with, and understood.
        </p>
        <p class="tags"><span>Naturalia</span><span>Artificialia</span><span>Scientifica</span></p>
      </section>

      <blockquote>
        <p>A collection was also a portrait of the person who <em>made it.</em></p>
        <footer>Taste · reach · curiosity · the limits of what one could know</footer>
      </blockquote>

      <section class="block">
        <p class="kicker">02 · When the shelves divided</p>
        <h2>Then the world got labelled.</h2>
        <p>
          Over time, collections became museums. Inquiry acquired disciplines, departments and names.
          The sorting made knowledge more exact, and easier to share.
        </p>
        <p>
          But a label can arrive too soon. Sometimes the most useful thing is to leave two unlike objects
          together long enough for a third idea to appear.
        </p>
        <p class="spine" aria-hidden="true"><span>wonder</span><span>specimen</span><span>discipline</span><span>?</span></p>
      </section>

      <section class="block">
        <p class="kicker">03 · The collector, now</p>
        <h2>I collect ideas. I collect experience.</h2>
        <p>
          I collect questions, places, stories, contradictions, people. Things that have no obvious reason
          to be beside one another, until they do.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="block">
        <p class="kicker">Loose specimens · 01 — 03</p>
        <h2>Curiosities, for now.</h2>
        <ol class="plates">
          {specimens.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <figure>
                <img src={s.src} alt={s.alt} />
                <figcaption>
                  <span>{s.no}</span>
                  <strong>{s.title}</strong>
                  {s.meta}
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="close">
        <p class="kicker">04 · What the cabinet is for</p>
        <h2>The meaning is in the between.</h2>
        <p>
          The work moves across architecture and data, technology and people, systems and stories.
          I am interested in what happens when unlike things meet, and in the meaning we make there, together.
        </p>
        <p class="end">A collection is never the whole world. It is one way of seeing it.</p>
        <p class="links"><a href="/writing">Step into the writing</a></p>
      </section>
    </RoomShell>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  html { overflow-y: auto; overflow-x: clip; }
  body { overflow-y: auto; overflow-x: clip; min-height: 100svh; color: var(--bone); }

  .kicker {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--champagne);
  }

  .open {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(11rem, 15rem);
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: end;
  }

  .display, h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .display {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 3.2vw, 3rem);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    max-width: 16em;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.7rem);
  }

  .block { margin-top: 5.2rem; }

  .block p, .close p {
    max-width: 38rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--flesh);
  }

  .block em { color: var(--bone); }

  .tags { display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; font-style: normal; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .tags span {
    border: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.55);
    padding: 0.4rem 0.55rem;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--champagne);
  }

  .hero-plate, .plates figure { margin: 0; }
  .hero-plate img, .plates img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 26rem;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  figcaption, blockquote footer {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--champagne);
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 4.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }

  blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 16em;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  blockquote em { font-style: italic; color: var(--bronze); }

  .spine {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.4rem;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 0.8rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.55);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--champagne);
  }

  .plates {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.2rem;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .plates img {
    height: 16rem;
    background: #070707;
    border: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.4);
  }

  .plates figcaption { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .plates strong {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: none;
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  .close { margin-top: 5rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.45); }
  .end { color: var(--bronze) !important; }

  .links { font-style: normal; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .links a { color: var(--champagne); text-decoration: none; }
  .links a:hover { color: var(--gold); }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .open, .plates { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hero-plate {
      max-width: 16rem;
      justify-self: center;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
